  "solution": "Factor the equation:\n\n\\[\n4x^3+5x^2-8x=0\n\\]\n\n\\[\nx(4x^2+5x-8)=0\n\\]\n\nSo one root is \\(x=0\\). The other two roots come from:\n\n\\[\n4x^2+5x-8=0\n\\]\n\nBy Vieta’s formula, the sum of all roots of a cubic \\(ax^3+bx^2+cx+d=0\\) is:\n\n\\[\n-\\frac{b}{a}\n\\]\n\nHere \\(a=4\\), \\(b=5\\), so the sum of all 3 roots is:\n\n\\[\n-\\frac{5}{4}=-1.25\n\\]\n\nThe answer is -1.25.",
